  "scope": "An owned source Kind API server and a second owned peer Kind API server host a source registry and two fixed candidate destination registries. The same source-to-approved-destination pair first transfers the inert artifact through an open baseline. After destination reset, the governed copier reads enrollment records from the source Kubernetes API and compares the exact endpoint pair. A peer-cluster ServiceAccount with get access to only the approved destination Service provides a current UID observation over a case-owned TLS endpoint. A separate approver binds that UID to the pair; replacing the Service invalidates the approval until refreshed. This tests one governed copier path, not third-party endpoint ownership or all replication routes.",
